# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HY-OS — what does not belong on GitHub
#
# The repo's job is the source: src/, build.py, deploy.sh and the small static
# assets the page references. Everything build.py produces, and everything that
# is not mine to publish, stays out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- music -----------------------------------------------------------------
# These are commercially released recordings, not my work. A public repo is a
# worse place for them than a bucket: it is indexed, it is permanent in the
# history, and a DMCA notice takes down the whole repository, not just a file.
# src/tracks.json still lists them, so a fresh clone builds a page whose player
# reports three missing files and falls back to the synthesiser — which is the
# correct behaviour for anyone but me.
music/
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.wav
*.flac
*.ogg

# --- build output ----------------------------------------------------------
# `python3 build.py` regenerates both of these from src/ every time, so they
# would only ever show up as 275 KB of noise in a diff. resume.jpg is extracted
# from src/body/12-resume-image.b64, which IS committed.
# Publishing with GitHub Pages instead of S3? Delete the index.html line — Pages
# needs the built file in the repo.
index.html
resume.jpg

# --- local leftovers -------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
shot-*.png
*.orig
*.rej

# --- macOS -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?

# --- editors / tooling -----------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.claude/

# --- python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# --- node (only if a tool ever needs it; the site itself uses none) ---------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# --- credentials and machine-local config ----------------------------------
# deploy.sh reads AWS credentials from `aws configure` (~/.aws), which is
# outside this folder — nothing secret should ever land here, but if a habit
# ever puts one here, it does not get committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
.aws/
